<%#
  Where you are in setup: a label over a three-segment rule.

  Not dots. An orange rule is already how this interface says "this is the
  one you are on" — it is the mark under the current page in the bar — so
  reusing it means the device needs no learning.

  Expects: step (1, 2 or 3), t.
-%>
<div>
  <span class="label"><%= t('setup.step', { current: step, total: 3 }) %></span>
  <div class="setup__progress">
    <%# The unescaped output tag is deliberate: run through the escaping one,
        a whole class attribute arrives as class=&quot;is-done&quot; and
        styles nothing at all. -%>
    <% for (let n = 1; n <= 3; n += 1) { %>
      <span<%- n <= step ? ' class="is-done"' : '' %>></span>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>
